    "body": "agent-note:v1\nstate: triaged\nlane: any-a\ntask: 17400\nissue: #10575\n\nTriaged inline by lane any-a (task 17400) at 2026-11-16T00:32Z. Issue #10575 is OPEN with no hard-stop labels. Work kind: small-fix (task/small-fix). Priority: priority/normal (keeper-filed completeness blocker for the Plans Space; no burn or routing impact). Effort: effort/s. Kind: kind/bug.\n\nRegistration decision (from the live code):\n- openrouter: REGISTERED POOL. It was enabled as a free-tier door on 2026-11-15 (commit b68f134124) and is measured ok with a real monthly window (pctOfLimit 0, resets 2026-12-01). It joins SHELL_POOLS in pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-extract.ts, mirroring the mistral shell-pool registration: identity-only in the dated view, live windows overlaid by overlayQuotaCurrent. The quota.test.ts assertion that extractQuotaPools emits no openrouter pool is updated deliberately: its premise was that openrouter was a disabled door with no pool answering to it; that premise ended with the 2026-11-15 enablement.\n- groq: REGISTERED NON-POOL SERVICE. Groq has no quota surface at all (failureClass no-quota-surface; rate limits exist only as inference-response headers / the console Limits page), so its gatherer row can never carry a window. It joins NON_POOL_SERVICE_IDS in pm-stack/aggregator/src/quota-current.ts, alongside turso/antigravity/opencode-go: the overlay will not synthesize an identity-only error pool for it. A gatherer-side change (not reporting an unmeasurable provider) stays with the quota-gatherer guardian, out of this task's scope.\n\nFirst concrete step: worktree fix adding both registrations plus the measured-provider census test for the 2026-11-16 tick (groq + openrouter) in quota-gather-map.test.ts.\nAcceptance check: census test passes for groq and openrouter; aggregator quota suites pass; the openrouter shell pool renders in extractQuotaPools and the groq row synthesizes no pool in overlayQuotaCurrent.\n",
